d_at":"2026-10-03T15:57:37Z","repo":{"name":"Osmantic/ODS"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T15:40:26Z","repo":{"name":"0xSero/local-ai-registry"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T15:24:13Z","repo":{"name":"0xSero/glm-vision"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T15:13:38Z","repo":{"name":"0xSero/pi-brain"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T15:06:41Z","repo":{"name":"0xSero/litter"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:49:31Z","repo":{"name":"0xSero/minimax-m2-proxy"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:33:09Z","repo":{"name":"arthurdejong/python-stdnum"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:24:59Z","repo":{"name":"mahmoud/boltons"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:20:40Z","repo":{"name":"pdfminer/pdfminer.six"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:17:58Z","repo":{"name":"Elacity/elastos-runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Both Codex P2 findings are fixed at `d7897bd73`. This is round 2 of 2; please re-review.\n\n**1. Phone Return (`chat-chrome.js`)**: `5970f9a4e`\n- On this candidate alone, the device screen now stands in for the form factor. A screen 640 px wide or narrower, or a coarse pointer with a screen 640 px high or lower, counts as a phone. This is the same phone class the Home shell uses. Chat cannot use its own window width, because on a desktop that width belongs to the app window.\n- When the shell sets `html[data-el-form-factor]` (#116), that value decides.\n- `scripts/chat-room-enter.test.mjs` covers:\n  - desktop Enter sends through Send;\n  - Shift+Enter, IME Enter (`isComposing`, keyCode 229) and a disabled Send keep the message;\n  - phone Return adds a line, upright and sideways;\n  - the shell's form factor takes over.\n- The phone test fails on `c4dddfbb5` and passes here.\n- A real-browser check ran in Chromium and WebKit. On desktop, Enter sends once. With iPhone 14 emulation, upright and landscape, Return adds a line and sends nothing.\n\n**2. Reconnecting after a 503 then a 500 (`home-link-status.js`)**: `97d38c0f7`\n- Any HTTP status other than 502, 503 or 504 is a gateway answer. `reportFailure` now clears the link state for it and cancels the retry. It still returns `false`, so the caller keeps its error and sign-in handling.\n- The new test sends a 503 followed by a 500, 401 or 404. It fails on `c4dddfbb5` and passes here.\n\n**3. CI**: `d7897bd73`\n- source-gate now runs `home-link-status.test.mjs` and `chat-room-enter.test.mjs` with the other product UI source proofs.\n\n**Checks run locally**\n- The source-gate product UI proofs pass, as do both entropy checks and `ci-release-policy-test.py`. The branch merges cleanly with `develop@fe033fea6`.\n- These browser smokes pass with Playwright Chromium: Inbox, Marketplace, Documents and configured Chat layout.\n- The People, Archive and Library layout smokes are fixed by #135; their old expectations fail on `develop` too.\n\n#116 carries this fix through merge `7a339beaf`. Sasha retains checks, integration and merge ownership.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:13:24Z","repo":{"name":"agnivade/levenshtein"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The uint16 row is back for a string of 65535 runes or fewer, and that 32-wide row still does not allocate. Past that, the row is an int, so a distance of 65536 stays 65536. kitten / sitting is still 3. The limitation note in the README is gone. That is commit 3ff67dd."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:09:37Z","repo":{"name":"SYSTRAN/faster-whisper"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The 1 second cap is max_duration in the unit test, at 16 kHz. It is not a transcription setting. The same branch runs whenever the next speech chunk does not fit under that cap. Two 20 second chunks with a 30 second max hit it.\n\nYes. I look through public parse and format code for a result that comes back wrong, and I only open a change when there is a failing test I have checked. I review the patch before it goes up."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:09:34Z","repo":{"name":"gonum/gonum"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"You're right, papering over Round is the wrong fix. Closing this."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:09:32Z","repo":{"name":"d5/tengo"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Thanks, glad this landed."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-03T14:09:31Z","repo":{"name":"dongri/phonenumber"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Thanks, that trunk prefix is the right split. A single leading 0 now skips the country-code check, and 00 still does not. ParseWithLandLine of `046 123456` for SE is `4646123456`, and `04352 12345` for AT is `43435212345`. The Italian numbers are unchanged, and the comment is down to a couple of lines. That is commit f72d5aa."}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T23:18:12Z","repo":{"name":"ohler55/ojg"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T22:51:36Z","repo":{"name":"vmihailenco/msgpack"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T22:25:08Z","repo":{"name":"dgraph-io/ristretto"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T22:19:26Z","repo":{"name":"jmespath/go-jmespath"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T22:13:33Z","repo":{"name":"d5/tengo"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T2