"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T19:04:49Z","repo":{"name":"oklog/ulid"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:54:25Z","repo":{"name":"rickb777/period"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:42:47Z","repo":{"name":"alecthomas/kong"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:37:16Z","repo":{"name":"jordan-wright/email"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:30:52Z","repo":{"name":"asaskevich/govalidator"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:22:08Z","repo":{"name":"caarlos0/env"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:11:16Z","repo":{"name":"agnivade/levenshtein"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T18:01:29Z","repo":{"name":"PuerkitoBio/purell"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:45:49Z","repo":{"name":"valyala/fastjson"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:41:24Z","repo":{"name":"collective/icalendar"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:23:01Z","repo":{"name":"c2h5oh/datasize"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:19:21Z","repo":{"name":"jinzhu/now"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T17:00:40Z","repo":{"name":"python-babel/babel"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:40:56Z","repo":{"name":"NVIDIA-NeMo/Run"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"A triple-quoted argument was dropped. list('''it's fine''', 2) came back empty because the apostrophe closed the quote. The splitter now keeps a ''' or \"\"\" quote together. That call is ['it's fine', 2], and list(\"\"\"a \"b\" c\"\"\", 3) is ['a \"b\" c', 3]. The quoted-comma cases are unchanged."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:38:01Z","repo":{"name":"lark-parser/lark"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The test is a TestCase now, and tests/__main__.py imports TestTextSlice. `python -m unittest tests.test_textslice` passed, 4 tests."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:37:31Z","repo":{"name":"bozhinov/pChart2.0-for-PHP7"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Ha, glad it was still worth a look. Thanks for merging it."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T16:37:29Z","repo":{"name":"distribution/reference"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The package tests pass. `go test ./...` is ok on this branch.\n\nThe red job is golangci-lint v2.0 typechecking Go 1.27. It cannot load crypto/sha256 (export data version 4, the linter supports 2), and then every digest use shows up as undefined. The oncevalue PR failed that same test job in April. I have not changed the linter. Happy to bump it in this PR if you want."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T12:48:49Z","repo":{"name":"redis/redis-py"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"You're right, #4308 covers this. It fixes both parsers and rejects the paths this one still ignored. I'll leave the fix there."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:53:16Z","repo":{"name":"Elacity/elastos-runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Fix candidate for the app-frame regression: #202, head `3bceced34`, based on develop `17132f05b` and merging cleanly with `829a24ad7`.\n\n#202 applies option (1). Home keeps `frame-ancestors 'none'`, and the Home GUI and CLI shells keep `frame-ancestors <Home origin>`. App and viewer documents rely on the response sandbox until #176 gives the Runtime-owned host direct control of app frames.\n\nProof:\n- `content_sandbox_browser` opens Home, the sandboxed shell and then Assistant and Marketplace from real gateway responses. It fails on develop and passes on #202.\n- A hostile page in the signed-in browser can display Assistant, while the gateway keeps the Home cookie, launch token and API authority with Home. The browser sends the frame request without the Home cookie, and unsigned API calls get 403.\n- A real signed-in Home on macOS, built from `3bceced34`, opens Marketplace and Assistant after Touch ID (video shared with Anders).\n\nCI: 8 of 9 checks pass. `source-home-linux (ubuntu-24.04)` stops at the Kubo download while dist.ipfs.tech is unreachable, and it re-runs when the site returns.\n\nDone means: option (1) replaces \"a foreign site still cannot frame an app\" with \"a foreign frame receives an opaque document, and Home keeps its cookie, launch token and API authority\". Please confirm this wording. Review: an independent ChatGPT review, and Irzhy for isolation.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T08:40:09Z","repo":{"name":"Elacity/elastos-runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Tested in a real signed-in Home on macOS, built from this PR's head `3bceced34` with `setup-source-home.sh` and `mac-source-home-restart.sh --init`, collaboration mode isolated.\n\n- Marketplace and Assistant both open inside the Home GUI shell after Touch ID sign-in.\n- Served headers match the change: `/home/` has `frame-ancestors 'none'`; `/apps/home-gui/` has sandbox and `frame-ancestors http://localhost:61190`; `/apps/marketplace/` and `/apps/assistant/` have sandbox and no `frame-ancestors`.\n- Unrelated to this PR: model download stops at the metadata read (`model_index_read` availability fallback fails; isolated mode has no Carrier peers while the public seed is paused). Browser needs the `browser-vm-image` component, which a source install doesn't include.\n\nCI: all checks pass except `source-home-linux (ubuntu-24.04)`, which fails twice at `local-carrier setup smoke` because the Kubo download from dist.ipfs.tech times out. The site is unreachable from here too; only the macOS job caches Kubo. I'll re-run it when the site is back.\n"}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T07:59:23Z","repo":{"name":"relvacode/iso8601"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Rebased onto current master. That picks up the golangci-lint v2.14.0 update."}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T07:21:46Z","repo":{"name":"Elacity/elastos-runtime"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T04:48:08Z","repo":{"name":"SYSTRAN/faster-whisper"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"That change is already on the branch. Commit 2d669276 takes the first chunk before the loop and starts the loop at the second. A chunk that does not fit is recorded as the start of the next group. The five tests in tests/test_collect_chunks.py passed again on that commit. Requesting another look."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T04:34:20Z","repo":{"name":"SYSTRAN/faster-whisper"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"I don't have a model.transcribe example that hits this. The failure is inside collect_chunks, when the next speech chunk does not fit under max_duration. I have not reproduced it from the public API, so I won't invent one.\n\nIf you only want a public-API repro, close this. If the simpler fix is preferred (collect the first chunk, then iterate from the second), I can do that instead."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T04:32:31Z","repo":{"name":"PyCQA/isort"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Thanks. Please go ahead. I'll leave the fix to you."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T04:32:43Z","repo":{"name":"NVIDIA/earth2studio"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"That sentence was wrong, and it should not have been on the PR. I reviewed the change before opening it. I have removed the line.\n\nThe float32 fix is unchanged. Happy for you to reopen it, or I can resubmit without that sentence if you prefer."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T04:32:33Z","repo":{"name":"NVIDIA/numbast"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The three calls in the issue are the demo. I don't have a larger Numba program around them.\n\n`_replace_placeholders(\"Pair<T, U>\", {\"T\": \"U\", \"U\": \"int\"})` comes back `Pair<int, int>`. The `U` that was just inserted gets replaced again.\n\n`_replace_placeholders(\"Tuple<T>\", {\"T\": \"int\"})` comes back `intuple<int>`. `T` matches the first letter of `Tuple`.\n\n`const T*` with `T=int` stays `const int*`."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-02T03:47:18Z","repo":{"name":"Elacity/elastos-runtime"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Closing as agreed with Anders. Invite links and QR codes stay out of the first user release (0.8.0), and the server currently refuses room joins (409), so these controls would only lead to a refusal. Invites come back as stages 2 and 3 of #86 once there is a server join path. The branch `fix/chat-invite-in-home-0.7.1-models` is kept."}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T16:20:56Z","repo":{"name":"MagicStack/py-pgproto"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T16:04:10Z","repo":{"name":"PyMySQL/PyMySQL"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T15:50:38Z","repo":{"name":"jquast/wcwidth"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T15:29:16Z","repo":{"name":"eliben/pycparser"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T15:22:17Z","repo":{"name":"life4/textdistance"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T15:09:35Z","repo":{"name":"kurtmckee/feedparser"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:39:56Z","repo":{"name":"celery/celery"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Yes. #10538 already covers abbr() going past max when max is shorter than the ellipsis. Closing this as a duplicate."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:39:51Z","repo":{"name":"python-babel/babel"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Yes. #1338 is the same noon and midnight parse. Closing this."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:39:49Z","repo":{"name":"SYSTRAN/faster-whisper"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"The 1 second figure is max_duration=1.0 in the test, at 16 kHz. It is not a transcription setting.\n\nThat branch runs whenever the next speech chunk does not fit under max_duration. With a 30 second max, two 20 second chunks hit it. The second chunk kept its audio and lost its segment list. A first chunk longer than max_duration also put an empty array in front."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:39:48Z","repo":{"name":"NVIDIA/kvpress"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Thanks. The diff is only get_exact_match now. The imports are back at the top of the file, and the test file is gone.\n\nI'm not running Loogle. I hit this while reading get_exact_match. An unparsed prediction was counted as 1 instead of the number of keys in the reference."}}},{"type":"IssueCommentEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:39:45Z","repo":{"name":"facelessuser/soupsieve"},"payload":{"action":"created","comment":{"body":"Thanks. The fix note is at the end of the 3.0 list, it cites (#307), and U+FFFD is in backticks in the changelog, the parser comment, and the test."}}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:32:31Z","repo":{"name":"chardet/chardet"},"payload":{"action":"opened"}},{"type":"PullRequestEvent","created_at":"2026-10-01T14:13:06Z","repo":{"name":"kennethreitz/records"},"payload